   "reply": "I added `Ledger.close(name)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`. It raises `ValueError` if the account's balance isn't zero. Otherwise it removes the account. The full suite passes (3 tests), including the new `test_close_requires_zero_balance` in `tests/test_ledger.py`.\n\nThat test transfers money into an account and checks that closing it fails and leaves it in place. It then transfers the money back and checks that closing succeeds.\n\nClosing an account that doesn't exist raises `KeyError`, the same as `balance()` does for an unknown name. You didn't specify this case, so I kept it consistent with the existing code.\n\nI ran the suite with `PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests`.",
